758	2. Create comprehensive test suites
759	3. Run tests and store failure patterns
760	4. Provide feedback to implementation agents
761	5. Document testing strategies in knowledge graph
762	
763	### Documentation Agent Actions
764	1. Wait for feature completion
765	2. Generate API documentation from code
766	3. Create user guides and examples
767	4. Store documentation patterns
768	5. Ensure consistency across project docs
769	
770	## 🔧 Tool Usage Priorities
771	
772	### Phase 1: Analysis (Always First)
773	1. \`analyze_project_structure(".")\` - Understand codebase
774	2. \`search_knowledge_graph(".", "relevant query")\` - Check existing knowledge
775	3. \`scrape_documentation()\` - Get external context if needed
776	
777	### Phase 2: Planning
778	1. \`create_task()\` - Define objectives
779	2. \`orchestrate_objective()\` - Break down complex work
780	3. \`join_room()\` - Set up coordination
781	
782	### Phase 3: Implementation
783	1. Agent-specific tools (\`spawn_agent()\`, specialized workflows)
784	2. \`store_knowledge_memory()\` - Continuous learning
785	3. \`send_message()\` - Cross-agent coordination
786	
787	### Phase 4: Validation
788	1. \`list_agents()\` - Check completion status
789	2. Review stored insights and learnings
790	3. Run tests and validate implementation
791	
792	## 💡 Best Practices
793	
794	### Always Do This
795	- Start complex tasks with \`orchestrate_objective()\`
796	- Use foundation sessions for cost optimization
797	- Store insights immediately when discovered
798	- Check existing knowledge before implementing
799	- Coordinate agents via shared rooms
800	
801	### Never Do This
802	- Implement without analysis phase
803	- Skip documentation scraping for new frameworks
804	- Ignore shared memory from other agents
805	- Start multiple agents without coordination
806	- Forget to store learnings for future agents
807	
808	### Foundation Session Optimization
809	- Use descriptive session IDs: "auth-system-v2-2024"
810	- Share sessions across related agents (85-90% cost reduction)
811	- Include version numbers for iterative development
812	- Name sessions after major features or epics
813	
814	## 🚀 Quick Start Checklist
815	
816	For any new complex task:
817	1. ✅ \`analyze_project_structure(".")\` - Understand the codebase
818	2. ✅ \`search_knowledge_graph(".", "task-related-query")\` - Check existing work
819	3. ✅ \`orchestrate_objective("clear objective", ".", {foundation_session_id: "descriptive-name"})\` - Coordinate implementation
820	4. ✅ \`join_room("task-coordination")\` - Monitor progress
821	5. ✅ \`store_knowledge_memory()\` - Document learnings throughout
822	
823	**Data Location**: \`~/.mcptools/data/\` (SQLite databases with agent coordination, shared memory, and knowledge graphs)
824	
825	🎯 **Core Principle**: Always use multi-agent orchestration for complex tasks. Single agents are for investigation and simple operations only.
826	<!-- zzZMCPToolsTypescriptzz END -->`;
