Auth0 MCP Server

A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server implementation that integrates Auth0 Management API 
with Claude Desktop, enabling AI-assisted management of your Auth0 tenant.
Usage: auth0-mcp-server [options] [command]

Auth0 MCP Server - Model Context Protocol server for Auth0 Management API

Options:
  -V, --version   output the version number
  -h, --help      display help for command

Commands:
  init [options]  Initialize the server (authenticate and configure)
  run [options]   Start the MCP server
  logout          Remove all stored Auth0 tokens from the system keychain
  session         Display current authentication session information
  help [command]  display help for command

Examples:
  npx @auth0/auth0-mcp-server init
  npx @auth0/auth0-mcp-server init --tools 'auth0_*' --client claude
  npx @auth0/auth0-mcp-server init --read-only --client claude
  npx @auth0/auth0-mcp-server init --tools 'auth0_*_applications' --client windsurf
  npx @auth0/auth0-mcp-server init --tools 'auth0_list_*,auth0_get_*' --client cursor
  npx @auth0/auth0-mcp-server init --auth0-domain <auth0-domain> --auth0-client-id <auth0-client-id> --auth0-client-secret <auth0-client-secret>
  npx @auth0/auth0-mcp-server run
  npx @auth0/auth0-mcp-server run --read-only
  npx @auth0/auth0-mcp-server session
  npx @auth0/auth0-mcp-server logout
  
  For more information, visit: https://github.com/auth0/auth0-mcp-server

